In short:

- Non-commercial use is free. You may share and adapt lemo-animi for
  non-commercial purposes, with credit: "lemo-animi by Lemomo (LemoLab)",
  a link to https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-animi and to the licence, and
  a note if you changed it. For films made with lemo-animi, the credit
  alone is enough: see Credit for Films below.

- Commercial use needs a commercial licence, except as the Additional
  Permission for Individual Creators below allows. This includes using films
  made with lemo-animi commercially, for example in advertising, client work,
  monetised channels or products. To ask for one, email
  lemomo.studio@gmail.com.

CREDIT FOR FILMS

When you publish a film made with lemo-animi, under CC BY-NC 4.0 or under the
permission below, it is enough to credit "lemo-animi by Lemomo (LemoLab)" in
the film or in its description. For films, Lemomo (LemoLab) waives the other
attribution requirements in Section 3(a) of CC BY-NC 4.0, including the links
to lemo-animi and to the licence and the note of changes. Sharing lemo-animi
itself, or an adapted version of it, still needs the full credit above.

ADDITIONAL PERMISSION FOR INDIVIDUAL CREATORS

This permission is given by Lemomo (LemoLab) in addition to CC BY-NC 4.0. It
is separate from and independent of CC BY-NC 4.0 (see Section 7(b) of that
licence) and does not change it: CC BY-NC 4.0 applies to lemo-animi
unmodified.

1. Who can use it. You can use this permission while both of these are true:
   (a) you are an individual acting for yourself. A company, partnership,
       trust, multi-channel network (MCN), studio, agency or other
       organisation cannot use it, and neither can an individual acting for
       one. An agreement with an MCN or agency does not by itself stop you,
       as long as the accounts are yours and you run them yourself;
   (b) your creator income for the last 12 months is no more than CNY 50,000.
       If more than half of that income was paid to you in currencies other
       than CNY, the limit is USD 7,000 instead.

2. What you may do. You may use lemo-animi to make films, publish them on
   accounts that you own and control (on social media, video and content
   platforms, and your own website or newsletter), and earn money from them
   there: platform advertising and revenue sharing, affiliate and shopping
   commissions, tips and gifts, memberships and paid content, and
   sponsorships you publish on your own accounts. This covers films made with
   any version of lemo-animi, including versions published before this
   permission.

3. What it does not cover.
   (a) Making films for a client or for anyone else, including films you hand
       over for someone else to publish or to use in their own advertising;
   (b) putting lemo-animi, or anything adapted from it, into a product or
       service for other people to use;
   (c) selling or sharing lemo-animi, or style packs, prompts or templates
       adapted from it, for commercial advantage;
   (d) third-party material, which keeps its own licence or terms. For
       example, narration made with Microsoft Edge online voices is under
       Microsoft's terms, and the instrument samples keep their own licences
       and credit requirements.
   Items (a) to (c) need a commercial licence.

4. Counting your income. "Creator income" is all the money, and the value of
   anything else, that you receive as a creator from all your accounts and
   channels, for any content, not only films made with lemo-animi. Count it
   before income tax and before your own costs, after any share that a
   platform keeps under its own rules. "The last 12 months" means the 12
   months before the day you check, so check again as you go. To compare
   income in another currency with the limit, use any reasonable exchange
   rate on or about the day you received it, for example the one your
   platform, bank or payment service used. A conversion made in good faith is
   enough.

5. When you go over. If your creator income goes over the limit, or you stop
   being an individual described in 1(a), you may keep using this permission
   for 30 days. To keep making films for commercial use after that, buy a
   commercial film licence (individual tier) within those 30 days. Films you
   published while you could use this permission stay covered: you may keep
   them online and keep earning from them, whether or not you buy a licence.
   If you were already over the limit on the day this section was added to
   this file, the 30 days start on that day.

6. Credit. Credit "lemo-animi by Lemomo (LemoLab)" in the film or in its
   description. No link is needed.

7. Nothing to apply for. You do not need to ask, register or report. If we
   ask, tell us in writing whether you meet the conditions above. We will not
   ask for your bank or tax records.

8. Terms. This permission is worldwide, royalty-free and non-exclusive. It is
   personal to you and cannot be transferred. For films published while you
   could use it, it is irrevocable. It applies to the extent that your use of
   lemo-animi needs permission from Lemomo (LemoLab). lemo-animi is provided
   as is, as Section 5 of CC BY-NC 4.0 says, to the extent the law allows.

Third-party material keeps its own licence:

